    <briefdescription>
<para>Policy Conflict Detection and Resolution Engine. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Detects and analyzes conflicts between policy rules with comprehensive conflict categorization, severity assessment, and resolution recommendations.</para>
<para><bold>Conflict Types:</bold><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>PERMIT-DENY: Same resource/action, conflicting effects</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Overlapping: Partially overlapping policies with no explicit precedence</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Circular Dependency: Policy chains forming cycles</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Type Mismatch: Incompatible rule types</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Precedence Algorithm (Deny-Overrides-Permit):</bold><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Evaluate all applicable rules for a request</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If ANY rule denies access -&gt; DENY (unless overridden by explicit precedence)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>If explicit precedence exists -&gt; follow priority order</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Otherwise -&gt; PERMIT (default allow)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Ties resolved by creation timestamp (earliest wins)</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para><bold>Atomic Updates:</bold> Policy updates validate for conflicts before committing. Failed updates roll back to previous state with full consistency guarantees.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="version"><para>0.1.0 </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="since"><para>2026-08-18 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
